load ../credential-region-materialization.maude

--- Fixture shape. One sealed value v1, an open request, a guard over it, and
--- an effect e1 that needs it. THE SAME FIXTURE IS RUN AGAINST ALL THREE
--- MODULES, which is the point: the designs are told apart by what they can
--- reach from identical starting conditions, not by different setups.

--- Coverage: under A', opening yields a binding and whip evaluates a guard
--- over the plaintext. This is the capability the collapse argument claimed
--- was lost.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-MATERIALIZATION :
  custody sealedVal(v1) openReq(v1) guardReq(v1) effectReq(e1, v1)
  =>* C:Cfg guardEvaluated(v1) .

--- Coverage: under A', the durable outbox row holds ciphertext.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-MATERIALIZATION :
  custody sealedVal(v1) openReq(v1) guardReq(v1) effectReq(e1, v1)
  =>* C:Cfg persistedCipher(v1) .

--- Coverage: under A', the worker opens the envelope during the run, so the
--- effect still receives the data it needs. Sealing the input is not a
--- functional restriction on the effect.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-MATERIALIZATION :
  custody sealedVal(v1) openReq(v1) guardReq(v1) effectReq(e1, v1)
  =>* C:Cfg runOpens(e1, v1) .

--- Coverage: negative fixture 1. Option A as originally written puts plaintext
--- in the outbox row, which is durable, so the plaintext is persisted. The
--- violation that motivated the rescue is real.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-MATERIALIZATION-OPENED-INPUT :
  custody sealedVal(v1) openReq(v1) guardReq(v1) effectReq(e1, v1)
  =>* C:Cfg persistedPlain(v1) .

--- Coverage: Option B is functional. The effect runs and the worker opens the
--- envelope, so B is a working design and not a degenerate one.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-MATERIALIZATION-NO-BINDING :
  custody sealedVal(v1) openReq(v1) guardReq(v1) effectReq(e1, v1)
  =>* C:Cfg runOpens(e1, v1) .

--- THEOREM C1. A' preserves T3: no durable record ever holds plaintext.
--- No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-MATERIALIZATION :
  custody sealedVal(v1) openReq(v1) guardReq(v1) effectReq(e1, v1)
  =>* persistedPlain(v1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- THEOREM C2. A' never puts opened content in an effect input at all, which
--- is the mechanism C1 rests on rather than a separate claim. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-MATERIALIZATION :
  custody sealedVal(v1) openReq(v1) guardReq(v1) effectReq(e1, v1)
  =>* effectInputOpened(e1, v1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- THEOREM C3. Option B cannot evaluate a guard over sealed content, from the
--- same fixture that reaches it under A'. Together with the first coverage
--- search this is the demonstration: A' and B are DISTINGUISHABLE, so the
--- claim that the rescued Option A "has become Option B" is false.
--- No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-MATERIALIZATION-NO-BINDING :
  custody sealedVal(v1) openReq(v1) guardReq(v1) effectReq(e1, v1)
  =>* guardEvaluated(v1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- THEOREM C4. The reason for C3, stated directly: under B plaintext never
--- enters whip's value space, so there is nothing to evaluate over. The
--- difference between A' and B is exactly this term. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-MATERIALIZATION-NO-BINDING :
  custody sealedVal(v1) openReq(v1) guardReq(v1) effectReq(e1, v1)
  =>* bound(v1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- THEOREM C5. B preserves T3 as well. This matters for the comparison: A' is
--- not safer than B, it is more expressive at equal safety, so the choice
--- between them is about language shape and not about the guarantee.
--- No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-MATERIALIZATION-NO-BINDING :
  custody sealedVal(v1) openReq(v1) guardReq(v1) effectReq(e1, v1)
  =>* persistedPlain(v1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: under A', sealing on the way into an effect input REQUIRES custody.
--- Without it nothing is lowered and nothing is persisted, so the crossing is
--- a real custodian operation rather than a local re-labelling. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-REGION-MATERIALIZATION :
  sealedVal(v1) openReq(v1) guardReq(v1) effectReq(e1, v1)
  =>* persistedCipher(v1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .
